# AGENTS.md — `scripts/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. Operator CLIs sit at trust
boundaries; inspect the command and its documented writes before invoking it.

## Permission boundary

- Read-only validation and setup that changes only ignored local state may run
  as part of an authorized task.
- Adding/moving raw data, `{{ data_versioning }} push`, registering a run,
  appending `metadata/runs.csv`, archiving registered provenance, adding a human
  lab-notebook interpretation, freezing a delivery, and uploading/mutating Lab
  Tracker records require explicit user approval.
- Approval for one named mutation does not authorize adjacent mutations.
- Never bypass idempotence, locks, conflict checks, atomic writes, or validation.
  On failure, report the error and verify durable state was not partially changed.
- Retrieve Git/DVC/run identities from their authoritative tools and files; do
  not fill missing fields with plausible values.

Keep reusable computation in `src/`; keep Snakemake adaptation in
`workflow/scripts/`. An operator CLI may call both, but it must make its side
effects visible at the command boundary.
